By decoupling the functional interface (id, commands, events, accepts) from the executing runtime (runtime, version), SDOA v5.0 allows individual modules to grow, optimize, and shift languages independently. The system transitions away from human-hardwired configurations into an automated marketplace where the most optimal asset is selected dynamically by a system of architectural sovereigns.  2. SDOA v5.0 Sovereign Role DirectoryTo govern a polyglot portfolio, SDOA v5.0 formally expands its static schema classification beyond basic module types (primitive, feature, adapter, service, workflow, repository) to include System Operational Roles. These roles dictate system-level behaviors, constraints, and execution priorities.  System Sovereigns (Infrastructure Layer)registrar (Registrar.service.js)Domain: System Topology Arbitration.Responsibility: Monitors portfolio directories for structural changes, reads manifest profiles, and resolves naming collisions. When multiple components claim identical functional identity paths, the registrar evaluates compiler matrices to prioritize the most optimal asset.captain (Captain.service.js)Domain: System State Sovereignty.Responsibility: Dictates application state transitions, handles global initializations, and manages fallback containment protocols when a runtime component fails or encounters an unhandled exception.conductor (Conductor.service.js)Domain: Multi-Module Event Coordination.Responsibility: Intercepts cross-module message passing across the universal EventBus. Evaluates the actions.events and actions.accepts manifest blocks to prevent event storms or circular logical deadlocks.  Cognitive & Defensive Sovereigns (Automation Layer)coach (Coach.workflow.py)Domain: Code Mutation Synthesis.Responsibility: Executed within a Python runtime to leverage native Abstract Syntax Tree (AST) tools, data parsing frameworks, and LLM orchestration providers. Evaluates runtime performance gaps or test runner failures to synthesize standalone, micro-incremented source code corrections.probation-officer (ProbationOfficer.workflow.rs)Domain: Structural Compliance & Isolation.Responsibility: Compiled to high-performance, memory-safe Rust code. Intercepts newly synthesized files before they are accepted into the live portfolio. Executes them within sandboxed WebAssembly (Wasm) boundaries to verify manifest contracts, enforce anti-pattern constraints, and catch errors prior to hot-reloading.  Mechanical Sovereigns (Execution Layer)assembly-line (AssemblyLine.service.js)Domain: Direct In-Memory Interop.Responsibility: Manages near-zero-overhead polyglot bindings. Configures SharedArrayBuffer structures and maps V8 typed arrays directly to shared native binary heaps, avoiding network overhead for intense computational processing.triage (Triage.workflow.js)Domain: Telemetry-Driven Routing.Responsibility: Intercepts incoming execution requests, evaluating parameter complexity, input data sizes, and CPU thread health to instantly stream tasks to the most efficient operational lane.3. The Canonical v5.0 Manifest StandardEvery module in an SDOA v5.0 portfolio must explicitly declare its profile via an identical, machine-readable manifest layout—regardless of source language.JavaScript// Last modified: 2026-06-01 15:30 UTC
// Formatted by Coach.workflow.py; Validated by ProbationOfficer.workflow.rs

static MANIFEST = {
  // ── Identity ──────────────────────────────
  id:              "MathSolver.engine",
  type:            "engine",
  layer:           3,
  runtime:         "Rust", // Browser | NodeJS | Universal | Rust | Python | C++ | COBOL | VB
  version:         "5.0.0",
  operationalRole: "savant", // registrar | captain | conductor | coach | probation-officer | assembly-line | triage | savant

  // ── Evolutionary Constraints ──────────────
  requires:        [], 
  dataFiles:       [],
  lifecycle:       ["init", "run", "dispose"],

  // ── Action Surface ────────────────────────
  actions: {
    commands: {
      transform: {
        description: "Executes vectorized floating-point matrix transformations.",
        input:  { matrix: "array" },
        output: "array"
      }
    },
    events:   {},
    accepts:  {},
    slots:    {}
  },

  // ── Metrics Optimization Target ───────────
  optimization: {
    priority: "speed", // speed | safety | readability | memory-footprint
    assertionSuite: "MathSolver.tests.json"
  },

  // ── Documentation ─────────────────────────
  docs: {
    description: "High-performance Rust execution unit targeted to WebAssembly via direct shared memory arrays.",
    author: "ProtoAI Core Architecture Group",
    sdoa: "5.0.0"
  }
};
